  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "buildah security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for buildah is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "The  package provides a command line tool which can be used to * create a working container from scratch or * create a working container from an image as a starting point * mount/umount a working container\u0026apos;s root file system for manipulation * save container\u0026apos;s root file system layer to create a new image * delete a working container or an image\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nSSH Agent servers do not validate the size of messages when processing new identity requests, which may cause the program to panic if the message is malformed due to an out of bounds read.(CVE-2025-47914)\n\nSSH servers parsing GSSAPI authentication requests do not validate the number of mechanisms specified in the request, allowing an attacker to cause unbounded memory consumption.(CVE-2025-58181)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for buildah is now available for master/openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP3/openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4/openEuler-24.03-LTS/openEuler-24.03-LTS-Next/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP2/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of medium. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Medium",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "buildah",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
